{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6hBrJUaAQCsxJjHcztM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that allows customers to cancel active orders, with order status tracking (ACTIVE, CANCELLED), idempotent cancellation of already-cancelled orders, atomic validation preventing cancellation when any shipment is CONFIRMED, and prevention of creating shipments for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order model: Order.kt:11-16 (no status field currently)\n- OrderController: OrderController.kt:15-46 (handles POST /orders, GET /orders/{orderId}, GET /orders)\n- OrderRepository: OrderRepository.kt:10-27 (in-memory store with save/findById/existsById/findAll)\n- Shipment model: Shipment.kt:9-14 (already has ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: ShipmentController.kt:20-56 (handles POST /shipments, GET /shipments/{shipmentId}, GET /shipments)\n- ShipmentRepository: ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27 (no method to find shipments by orderId)\n- Error handling: ApiExceptions.kt:11-30, ApiError.kt:31-37 (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409), GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- ApiException subclasses thrown from controllers/services, caught by GlobalExceptionHandler, converted to ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- 201 for creation, 200 for retrieval, 404 for not found (ResourceNotFoundException), 409 for conflict (ConflictException)\n- Data classes for domain models, ResponseEntity for status codes\n- MockMvc tests validate both HTTP status and error envelope structure ($.error.code, $.error.message)\n\n**Affected files:**\n- Order.kt: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class\n- OrderController.kt: Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to retrieve all shipments for an order\n- ShipmentController.kt: Add validation to reject creating shipments for CANCELLED orders\n- ApiError.kt: Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code if needed for shipment creation rejection\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Add tests for cancel endpoint behavior (success, idempotency, CONFIRMED conflict, not found, shipment creation prevention)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Existing tests breaking due to Order model change (need to ensure backward compatibility in serialization or update test setup)\n- Race conditions in concurrent cancel operations (ConcurrentHashMap mitigates but operations must be atomic where possible)\n- Shipment status checks must happen atomically to prevent CONFIRMED shipments from being cancelled\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None identified that would change the design.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status: OrderStatus` field to Order. Default new orders to ACTIVE. This requires modifying the Order data class to include the status field.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order or throws ResourceNotFoundException (ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n   - If already CANCELLED, succeeds and returns it (idempotency)\n   - Loads all shipments for this order\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException (need new error code or reuse ORDER_ACTIVE_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n   - Otherwise, update order to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, save both, return updated order (201 Created or 200 OK - need to decide)\n   \n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to return all shipments for a given order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: In POST /shipments endpoint, before creating shipment, check if order exists and is CANCELLED. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (ORDER_CANCELLED or SHIPMENT_CANCELLED_ORDER).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for shipment creation on cancelled order)\n   - Or reuse `CONFLICT_` pattern\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling an already-CANCELLED order succeeds and returns 200 (idempotency)\n   - Cancelling an order with CONFIRMED shipments returns 409 with unchanged state\n   - Cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n   - Creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n**Alternative approaches rejected:**\n- Service layer: Could add OrderService for business logic, but the existing code has logic directly in controllers, so keeping it there maintains consistency.\n- Status enum placement: Could put OrderStatus in a shared constants file, but keeping it with Order model maintains cohesion.\n- HTTP response code for successful cancel: The ticket says \"returns the order\" - typically 200 OK for success, or 201 Created if treating as resource creation. The existing POST /orders returns 201 Created. For idempotency and consistency with successful operations, using 200 OK is standard for updates. But the requirement says \"Cancelling an `ACTIVE` order moves it to `CANCELLED`, returns the order\" - this is consistent with 200 OK (successful modification), not 201 (creation).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderController finds order (OrderRepository.findById) → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n3. Load shipments (ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId)\n4. Check no CONFIRMED shipments → none found\n5. Update order to CANCELLED, update shipments to CANCELLED\n6. Save both (OrderRepository.save, ShipmentRepository.save for each)\n7. Return 200 OK with updated Order\n\nCase 2: Cancel already-CANCELLED order\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderController finds order → Order(status=CANCELLED)\n3. Load shipments → found\n4. No CONFIRMED shipments\n5. Order already CANCELLED → return 200 OK unchanged (idempotent)\n\nCase 3: Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment present\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderController finds order → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n3. Load shipments → ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED found\n4. Throw ConflictException (with code ORDER_ACTIVE_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches → ResponseEntity.status(409).body(ApiError(...))\n6. Order and shipments unchanged\n\nCase 4: Cancel non-existent order\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderController finds order → null\n3. Throw ResourceNotFoundException (ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler catches → ResponseEntity.status(404).body(ApiError(...))\n\nCase 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order\n1. POST /shipments (orderId=cancelled-order)\n2. ShipmentController checks if shipment exists (OK) and order status\n3. Find order (OrderRepository.findById)\n4. Check order.status == CANCELLED\n5. Throw ConflictException (ORDER_CANCELLED)\n6. GlobalExceptionHandler catches → ResponseEntity.status(409).body(ApiError(...))\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `testCancelActiveOrderSucceeds`: Create order (ACTIVE), verify it's ACTIVE, cancel it, verify returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n2. `testCancelActiveOrderCancelsCreatedShipments`: Create order, create shipment (CREATED), cancel order, verify shipment is now CANCELLED\n3. `testCancelAlreadyCancelledOrderSucceeds`: Create order, cancel it, cancel again, verify returns 200 and nothing changed (idempotent)\n4. `testCancelWithConfirmedShipmentFails`: Create order, create shipment and confirm it, attempt cancel, verify 409 CONFLICT, verify order still ACTIVE, verify shipment still CONFIRMED\n5. `testCancelNonExistentOrderReturns404`: Attempt cancel on non-existent order, verify 404 NOT_FOUND with error envelope\n6. `testCreateShipmentForCancelledOrderFails`: Create order, cancel it, attempt to create shipment, verify 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n7. `testCancelOrderWithMultipleShipments`: Create order, create multiple shipments with different statuses, verify only CREATED are cancelled\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start implementing the changes. First, I'll add the OrderStatus enum and modify the Order model:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1629,"cache_read_input_tokens":17796,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1629},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fbe0d1b-83e5-4b93-9394-c97899d21215","uuid":"be6d8d15-0629-49a6-ba24-c2fa880bfd54","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:05:47.477Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6hBqjzVV1TdJXVmuJSe"}
